# R42 tail-reserve boundary cell.
#
# The EXPLODED comment-bearing path. An interior comment routes this list away
# from the fill packer and into the hand-rolled one-element-per-line emitter,
# which writes a `,` after EVERY element — including the last. Each element is
# therefore rendered under an EXACT reserve of 1: exact, not additive, because
# a live caller reserve belongs to the CLOSE line and charging it here would
# over-reserve every element line by ~25 columns.
#
# BOUNDARY PAIR: the first entry is 119 columns plus its comma = exactly 120
# and stays flat; the second is 120 plus its comma = 121 and breaks.
#
# RED, recorded against the PRE-FIX binary built from this track's own base
# commit: the second entry formats to a single 121-column line.
#
# TWO residuals, named rather than implied — this path is a hand-rolled loop
# with no `Doc::Fill` and no fit test anywhere, so NOTHING enforces a width on:
#   * the CLOSE line (`    ]` below, 5 columns) plus whatever the caller writes
#     after it. Outer indent + close + suffix is short in every real shape; a
#     hypothetical overrun there is out of scope and is not enforced.
#   * a trailing comment on an element line (`1,    # one`) — the comment's
#     width is never charged, by the same never-reflow-prose doctrine that
#     exempts standalone comments.

int probe_entry(int a, int b, int c, int d, int e): 0

void main():
    Vector[int] table = [
        # a leading interior comment routes this list to the exploded path
        probe_entry(1111111111, 2222222222, 3333333333, 4444444444, probe_entry(11111, 22222, 33333, 44444, 555555555)),
        probe_entry(1111111111, 2222222222, 3333333333, 4444444444, probe_entry(11111, 22222, 33333, 44444, 5555555559)),
        probe_entry(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),
    ]
    print(table.len())
